{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/735871-questions-about-spiritual-reflection-and-backgrounds","id":735871,"title":"Questions about spiritual reflection and Backgrounds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-28T14:40:45-07:00","id":735871,"title":"Questions about spiritual reflection and Backgrounds","content":"Hi everybody,<br /> <br /> It\u2019s my first post here. I\u2019ve seen plenty of useful stuff being discussed here with a lot of people involved in WW rules and background.<br /> <br /> So maybe you\u2019ll be able to help me. I\u2019m mastering a PBF (Play by Forum) campaign, and I have 2 questions which nobody was really able to give me answers about it everywhere I asked about it.<br /> <br /> The first question is about the eventually spiritual reflection of supernatural beings.<br /> So in W20 p313 we have this: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Penumbral streets and forests seem eerily empty, since most sentient creatures don\u2019t appear in the Penumbra. Only spiritually advanced people appear here. Mages have highly developed spiritual selves called Awakened Avatars, and their Avatars are visible in the Penumbra (even though each exists in the same realm as its mage). An animal won\u2019t appear visible in the Penumbra, but when many animals live and thrive in one place, an animal-spirit might be drawn to that locale\u2019s reflection in the Penumbra. </div> </div> </div>But would it be something for the other supernatural beings? I didn\u2019t find anything at the moment.<br /> <br /> My other question is more a mechanics question.<br /> As I said I\u2019m doing it on a forum. So I was wondering how will I use the Backgrounds that are working per game session like Ancestors? (You have to know that PBF is really MUCH MORE slower than a normal playing) I\u2019ve found these possibilities but I don\u2019t know which one to use.<br /> <br /> <br /> Real time? (Which would in the end tend to be the most close of a real game session, but then how much? A scene can stay for 2 weeks or even more\u2026 Depending of the players activity)<br /> In Game time? (Then again, how much use/how much time should I allow for the background to be useful without being useless or overpowered?)<br /> Per Story? (Then again, how much use/Story time should I allow for the background to be useful without being useless or overpowered?)<br /> <br /> <br /> PS : It's probably not perfect, English is my second language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T19:13:12-07:00","id":736516,"title":"","content":"Really as the ST it is your call on the umbra thing, mages have an avatar rating so if one has a really high avatar they should, by the example listed shine like a beacon in the umbra. <br /> <br /> So if for example you want a vampire to show up it might be a pale whisp outline of a person, but really it's your call.<br /> <br /> For the ancestors background I would just go until the scene is resolved and you move onto the next scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T23:26:57-07:00","id":737104,"title":"","content":"Welcome, and congrats on taking on the role of the storyteller!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/735871-questions-about-spiritual-reflection-and-backgrounds?p=736516#post736516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if for example you want a vampire to show up it might be a pale whisp outline of a person, but really it's your call.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the vampire is really perverse or prone to violence, there could easily be a few weak banes trailing in its wake, feeding off the ambient suffering.<br /> <br /> I also struggled a bit with what I first wanted the umbra to look like in my game. The books give you guidelines, but a lot is up to you as an individual. Since the umbra can look like nearly anything, just flesh it out in a way that appeals to you and supports the story. How you portray the spirit world in a given local will tell your players a lot, and unusual descriptions are a lot of fun. I rarely make my spirits look like just animals/objects. A spirit associated with bear might be a wild looking man, his rough hands and beard slathered with honey. A tree spirit that that native peoples held war councils under for generations might have its hide studded with arrows and lances, its roots watered in blood. Have fun with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T06:49:04-07:00","id":737975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Welcome, and congrats on taking on the role of the storyteller! </div> </div> </div>Thank you ! I'm having a lot of fun !<br /> <br /> Thanks also for the answers about the eventually Spiritual reflection. In the end it's really up to me, and as for the Mage i think i'll use it only for potent being that have a deep influence where they are.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the use of Ancestor it's more how often i should allow the players to use in, and on which scale of time. As we are by forum it's barely impossible to do it by game sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T03:26:54-07:00","id":741243,"title":"","content":"I would suggest that 99.9% of people shouldn't have any reflections in the Umbra.<ul><li>Vampires are broken and dead, and I really love the idea of Banes trailing behind them feeding on the misery the worst of them inflict.</li> <li>Mages usually won't show up, but having their avatars or echoes of their will working flash when they do something dramatic could be pretty cool.</li> <li>I'd apply the same guideline to the echoes of Changelings in the Umbra.</li> <li>Wraiths exist in a different Umbra that the Werewolves don't usually interact with, but occasionally they show up in the penumbra, and for the purposes of Werewolf they are just another spirit.</li> <li>Kuei Jin probably don't exist in the Umbra when they are in the real world, but they are dual beings like the Garou, so they can pop over and say hi. Devil Tigers and Scorpion Eaters could be trailed by Garou, but I'd play up the fact that the ones behind Scorpion Eaters are a bunch of maniacs driven to destroy and corrupt, while the ones behind the Devil TIgers would be frustrated and cowed due to their attitude</li> <li>Mummies... don't exist in the Umbra by default, but they can split apart their souls and send them into the Umbra and the Dark Umbra so I guess that'd be something you could encounter</li> <li>Demons. Demons are an interesting case, and I feel that Demons are so wrong and unnatural to the fabric of the world that the Umbra around them grows weird and wrong with echoes of the Demon's apocalyptic form showing up in the Umbra</li> </ul><br /> <br /> As for powers &quot;per session&quot; on your forum game, may i suggest you marking them as &quot;per story&quot; and then allowing them say 2-3 uses per story? That will make the powers special enough and the game temp won't give them infinite (ab)use of the power. Mind you in a forum game powers like that are narrative enough that you could probably go with just skipping the limit. Since you're new at the whole thing, I suggest giving them 2-3 uses for now and seeing how it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T04:37:39-07:00","id":744212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/735871-questions-about-spiritual-reflection-and-backgrounds?p=741243#post741243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would suggest that 99.9% of people shouldn't have any reflections in the Umbra.<ul><li>Vampires are broken and dead, and I really love the idea of Banes trailing behind them feeding on the misery the worst of them inflict.</li> <li>Mages usually won't show up, but having their avatars or echoes of their will working flash when they do something dramatic could be pretty cool.</li> <li>I'd apply the same guideline to the echoes of Changelings in the Umbra.</li> <li>Wraiths exist in a different Umbra that the Werewolves don't usually interact with, but occasionally they show up in the penumbra, and for the purposes of Werewolf they are just another spirit.</li> <li>Kuei Jin probably don't exist in the Umbra when they are in the real world, but they are dual beings like the Garou, so they can pop over and say hi. Devil Tigers and Scorpion Eaters could be trailed by Garou, but I'd play up the fact that the ones behind Scorpion Eaters are a bunch of maniacs driven to destroy and corrupt, while the ones behind the Devil TIgers would be frustrated and cowed due to their attitude</li> <li>Mummies... don't exist in the Umbra by default, but they can split apart their souls and send them into the Umbra and the Dark Umbra so I guess that'd be something you could encounter</li> <li>Demons. Demons are an interesting case, and I feel that Demons are so wrong and unnatural to the fabric of the world that the Umbra around them grows weird and wrong with echoes of the Demon's apocalyptic form showing up in the Umbra</li> </ul><br /> <br /> As for powers &quot;per session&quot; on your forum game, may i suggest you marking them as &quot;per story&quot; and then allowing them say 2-3 uses per story? That will make the powers special enough and the game temp won't give them infinite (ab)use of the power. Mind you in a forum game powers like that are narrative enough that you could probably go with just skipping the limit. Since you're new at the whole thing, I suggest giving them 2-3 uses for now and seeing how it goes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for all these nice ideas ! (and i definitely like the idea for the vampire also).<br /> <br /> After reading this I agree. Someone told me 1 time per sotyr but it\u2019s a bit cheapskate seeing how long can take a scenario (my Rite of Passage started in May 2014 and is going to finish soon). So yes. 2/3 time per story sound really ok in my mind. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T05:10:51-07:00","id":744262,"title":"","content":"Remember that ancestor-spirits can be visible as well in the umbra, especially around those they are bound to by such merits as Ancestor Ally. Also players with points in Fate or similar backgrounds should have some curious spirits who keep tabs on them. And as someone wrote about earlier, spirits aren't all easy to identify, there is a reason why there are gifts for that. Identifying a spirit as something different than it's true nature can lead to some great roleplaying moments in my experience.<br /> <br /> I agree with the limited time/story idea, but I think you should limit it to players rating (number of dots) per story as far as setting a limit for it.<br /> <br /> Just my 2 cents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9021-jeremiah-songkeeper","name":"Jeremiah Songkeeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}